Z||000003||Zoom88||12-08-2001||11:53 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>It <I>may</I> still be available through GM. I'll have to check w/ my local Pontiac dealership were I get all the new parts I can (they even give me the parts at their cost because I buy so much Fiero stuff from them!).<BR>I say that because I just bought 4 brand new side marker lights (all 4 corners) for my 87 GT...the rounded kind, brand new!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Pleeeze let me Know what you find out !!!!!<BR> Email me if you don't mind...<BR>  Thanks<P><p>[This message has been edited by Zoom88 (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||12-08-2001||11:54 PM||||The sidemarkers are still available ($25 retail....OUCH!), but some of the regular moldings are long gone.<P>LMK if you can come up with them though.....I too would be interested in them.||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnF||12-09-2001||08:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Zoom88:<BR><B> I would like to purchase a complete set new round moulding, <BR>(edited 12-08-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>There is no such thing!  <P>The side pieces are individually replaceable  The front and rear bumper pieces are a moulded part of the bumper covers.<P>So, you can find the side pieces but have to replace the entire bumper covers to replace the end pieces.<P>As to "new", what difference does it make?<P>||||reg||9
Z||000006||WampusCat||12-09-2001||08:57 AM||||The round moldings are NOT molded into the front fascia like the ribbed ones are.  The pointy "arrow heads" are replaceable and the marker light covers the rest of the fascia back to the wheel well.  <A HREF="http://www.partszoneonline.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.partszoneonline.com/</A>  has the fascia molding for $3.80 each. GM part #'s are<BR>10035764 (R) and 10035765 (L). <A HREF="http://www.parts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.parts.com</A>  has them for approx $5 each + shipping.  Fiero Store or your local dealer should have the marker light assembly.<P>This applies to round molding GT's.  I don't know how the coupes are put together.  I think the rear bumper does have the molding as a non-removeable part.<p>[This message has been edited by WampusCat (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Zoom88||12-09-2001||09:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WampusCat:<BR><B>The round moldings are NOT molded into the front fascia like the ribbed ones are.  The pointy "arrow heads" are replaceable and the marker light covers the rest of the fascia back to the wheel well.  <A HREF="http://www.partszoneonline.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.partszoneonline.com/</A>  has the fascia molding for $3.80 each. GM part #'s are 10035764 (R) and 10035765 (L). <A HREF="http://www.parts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.parts.com</A>  has them for approx $5 each + shipping.  Fiero Store or your local dealer should have the marker light assembly.<P>This applies to round molding GT's.  I don't know how the coupes are put together.  I think the rear bumper does have the molding as a non-removeable part.<P>[This message has been edited by WampusCat (edited 12-09-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks Wampus cat and everyone else with the positive replies, .....sorry  JohnF the difference is PERFECTION, QUALITY WORK, LOOKS I guess it all depends on what one is looking for, I personally want the best I can find, I plan on keeping this car a Looooooong time, Long time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||JohnF||12-09-2001||10:14 AM||||My orginal answer applied to only roughly HALF of the Fieros out here.  The front on my '88 coupe has a moulded-in round trim piece that is a black painted portion of the front bumpber cover.  The side pieces are replaceable without replacing the entire bumper.  The front isn't.<P>The front of my GT has no trim except the side pieces which are individually replaceable.<P>The rear of both models has moulded-in trim pieces.  Entire bumper cover must be replaced to replace the factory installed trim.  The rear trim is just a black painted portion of the moulded cover.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=57211671&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||11
